"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[53397],{4594:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"EnergyCannonServer","desc":"Authority for the train-mounted Energy Cannon (one heat-driven laser, hold to fire).\\nThe shared turret core (`TrainTurretServer`) discovers placed turrets, seats the\\ngunner after validation and steps yaw/pitch toward the gunner\'s aim reports. This\\nscript is the weapon on top of it: heat, overheat and the beam damage tick.\\n\\nHeat (`EnergyCannonMath.stepHeat`) rises while the beam is on and falls while it is\\noff; at 1 the cannon overheats and stays off until heat has cooled to 0, even with\\nthe trigger still held. Beam width and damage per second follow heat\\n(`EnergyCannonMath`). Every `1 / TickRate` seconds the server spherecasts from its\\nown muzzle (server yaw/pitch plus rig math, never the client\'s origin) along the\\ngunner\'s aim clamped into `AimConeDeg` around the barrel, and the FIRST thing hit\\nends the beam: an enemy takes the tick\'s damage (`TrainWeaponDamage.applyDirect`),\\na rock takes it through `RockService.Damage`; terrain or the train just stop it.\\nRocks have no server parts, so the cast runs next to `RockService.SegmentHit` and\\nthe nearer hit wins.\\n\\nThere is no per-tick packet. State is published as attributes on the placed Model:\\nFiring, Heat (throttled), Overheated, AimYaw, AimPitch, GunnerUserId, plus the HUD\\ncontract DisplayName, MaxHeat, PeakHeat (read by the generic TurretGui). Every client\\ndraws the beam from those.\\n\\nWith no gunner and a Smart Cannon / Orbital Sentinel holder in the party, the turret\\ntracks the nearest visible enemy (core auto-aim) and fires the beam while the barrel\\nis on target, at `AutoLoaderRate` x damage, credited to the holder. It heats and can\\noverheat like a manned cannon.","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":32,"path":"src/ServerScriptService/EnergyCannonServer.server.luau"}}')}}]);